  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "IANA-IP: Fix missing braces.",
  "description": "The braces in the data structures in epan/iana-ip-data.c are ... numerous.  And\nthere's a section where we switch off the \"missing-braces\" diagnostic with a\ncomment suggesting that GCC has a problem here.\n\nGCC appears to be correct; We were actually missing some braces, but Clang\naccepted it without complaint.\n\nAdd the braces and remove the deactivation of the compiler diagnostic.  Both\nGCC and Clang seem to accept the result.\n\nTo explain: The ipv6 field is a struct of type ipv6_addr_and_prefix; the\ninitializer for that struct is already demarcated by braces.  The first field\nof that struct is of type ws_in6_addr, also a struct; a set of braces already\ndemarcates that initializer too.  The sole element of that struct is an array\nof 16 bytes; initialization of that array requires braces, but those were\nmissing.",
  "state": "merged",
